{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c43b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07573-a73b-7be0-abe2-6029bca74ffd"},"sequence":120,"recorded_at":1780531400000235,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"65c281d8-14aa-4def-b705-62e70b4fce66","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"65c281d8-14aa-4def-b705-62e70b4fce66","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"65c281d8-14aa-4def-b705-62e70b4fce66"},"call_id":"call_01a07573e0f87163981047db0d186bb2","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3drr2m/worktree/internal/dirnode/doc.go`.\n1|// Package dirnode implements the ax host side of the companion\n2|// Directory Node protocol of pinned specification Section 7.9: the\n3|// two-major bootstrap, envelope framing, manifest and probe\n4|// validation, scan/inventory request framing with (operation,\n5|// operation_id) idempotency, Session Directory Query framing of\n6|// Section 10.8.5, façade binding checks, and Structured Error\n7|// 1.2.0 refusals.\n8|//\n9|// The actor every Section 7.9 RFC 2119 keyword governs here is the ax\n10|// host (this repository). The directory node is a child surface this\n11|// package never trusts: it runs in the same per-environment\n12|// implementation as Provider 2 and Session Adapter 1, and every byte\n13|// it emits is attacker-influenced, so every frame is validated\n14|// before any member is used. Neither major adds operations to\n15|// Provider 2, executes Continuation Plans, or transports\n16|// transcript/workspace bytes, and this host never asks for any of\n17|// those through this package.\n18|//\n19|// Major negotiation is caller-driven enumeration, not a hello: the\n20|// caller attempts its locally supported majors in strictly\n21|// descending order with one manifest request each, each attempt on a\n22|// fresh process. Only the exact downgrade tuple — one well-framed\n23|// failure echoing the request, response schema_version 1.0.0,\n24|// Structured Error 1.2 incompatible_protocol with exit 6 and\n25|// retryable=false, then process exit 6 — authorizes the next lower\n26|// attempt. Deciding that tuple is DecideBootstrapStep; launching and\n27|// reaping processes belongs to the caller, which records each\n28|// attempt's process token in a ProcessGuard so a returned or failed\n29|// process is never reused for a lower major.\n30|//\n31|// A failed read is never an absence: a partial, malformed,\n32|// over-limit, mislabeled, or escaped result is an\n33|// adapter_protocol_violation or transport_failure, never an empty\n34|// result and never fallback permission. A syntactically valid frame\n35|// naming an unknown operation is operation_unknown, refused\n36|// locally before any node surface is touched. Query framing\n37|// defects are query_invalid.\n38|//\n39|// Stated bounds: transport process management (spawning the node\n40|// executable, deadlines, stdio ownership, allowlist/SSH admission)\n41|// belongs to the caller, which supplies frames this package\n42|// validates as bytes; the content of nested observation and lineage\n43|// types owned by Sections 10.8 and 13.14 (EnvironmentObservation,\n44|// NativeSessionObservation, InventoryBatch, PreviewExcerpt payload\n45|// meaning, EnrichmentJobRequest/Receipt chains, ManagementBinding\n46|// content, RuntimeExpectation) is checked for presence and object\n47|// shape only — the shared-environment leaf of this Story owns that\n48|// content, and inventing its validation here would collide with that\n49|// ownership at integration. The scan journal in this package is an\n50|// in-memory (operation, operation_id) record with byte export and\n51|// import so crash recovery is demonstrable; its durable placement is\n52|// the core's property. Caller authentication (CallerContext is\n53|// authenticated server-side, never accepted from an unverified body\n54|// alone) belongs to the caller: this package validates the context\n55|// shape. Section 10.8.5 prose names a query_cursor_mismatch code the\n56|// pinned error registry does not register; cursor reuse after a\n57|// bound change is refused here as query_invalid with a\n58|// cursor-mismatch detail, and the divergence is recorded on the\n59|// refusing call site, not hidden.\n60|package dirnode","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c43d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07573-a73b-7be0-abe2-6029bca74ffd"},"sequence":121,"recorded_at":1780531400000237,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"65c281d8-14aa-4def-b705-62e70b4fce66","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"65c281d8-14aa-4def-b705-62e70b4fce66","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"65c281d8-14aa-4def-b705-62e70b4fce66"},"call_id":"call_01a07573e240736287fa42c9ebdc2683","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3drr2m/worktree/internal/dirnode/protocol.go`.\n1|package dirnode\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"bytes\"\n5|\t\"encoding/json\"\n6|\n7|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axerror\"\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n9|)\n10|\n11|// Wire constants of pinned specification Section 7.9. Directory\n12|// Node protocol 2.0.0 is the current separately negotiated\n13|// read-mostly façade; 1.0.0 remains an immutable legacy wire\n14|// contract. Neither major is a negotiation: a different major is an\n15|// invalid envelope, never a downgrade, except through the exact\n16|// manifest downgrade tuple DecideBootstrapStep recognizes.\n17|const (\n18|\t// ProtocolID is the exact protocol member every request and\n19|\t// response envelope carries.\n20|\tProtocolID = \"urn:ax:protocol:session-directory-node\"\n21|\t// RequestSchema is the exact schema member every request\n22|\t// envelope carries.\n23|\tRequestSchema = \"urn:ax:schema:session-directory-node-request\"\n24|\t// ResponseSchema is the exact schema member every response\n25|\t// envelope carries. The response carries its own schema\n26|\t// member because the downgrade tuple names a response\n27|\t// schema_version distinct from every echoed request member;\n28|\t// a response without one cannot carry that tuple.\n29|\tResponseSchema = \"urn:ax:schema:session-directory-node-response\"\n30|\t// ManifestSchema is the exact schema identifier the manifest\n31|\t// body carries.\n32|\tManifestSchema = \"urn:ax:schema:session-directory-node-manifest\"\n33|\t// ManifestSchemaVersion is the only manifest version this host\n34|\t// accepts under either major.\n35|\tManifestSchemaVersion = \"1.0.0\"\n36|\t// ResponseSchemaVersion is the only response schema_version\n37|\t// this host accepts under either major: both majors bind\n38|\t// Directory Node Response 1.0.0.\n39|\tResponseSchemaVersion = \"1.0.0\"\n40|\t// MajorV1 is the legacy wire major.\n41|\tMajorV1 = 1\n42|\t// MajorV2 is the current wire major.\n43|\tMajorV2 = 2\n44|\t// ErrorVersion is the Structured Error version every failure\n45|\t// envelope carries: Directory Node 1 and 2 statically bind\n46|\t// Structured Error 1.2.0.\n47|\tErrorVersion = axerror.Version120\n48|\t// MaxFrameBytes bounds one JSONL line in either direction:\n49|\t// Section 7.9 inherits the rule that every line is one\n50|\t// complete UTF-8 JSON object no larger than 8 MiB.\n51|\tMaxFrameBytes = 8 << 20\n52|\t// MinDeadlineMS and MaxDeadlineMS bound deadline_ms to\n53|\t// uint53[1..3600000].\n54|\tMinDeadlineMS = uint64(1)\n55|\tMaxDeadlineMS = uint64(3600000)\n56|)\n57|\n58|// supportedMajors is the single construction site of the local\n59|// major registry, in strictly descending numeric order: peers\n60|// choose the highest mutually supported major.\n61|var supportedMajors = []int{MajorV2, MajorV1}\n62|\n63|// SupportedMajors returns the locally supported Directory Node\n64|// majors in strictly descending numeric order. The result is a\n65|// copy; the registry cannot be mutated through it.\n66|func SupportedMajors() []int {\n67|\treturn append([]int(nil), supportedMajors...)\n68|}\n69|\n70|// VersionForMajor binds a supported major to its exact N.0.0 wire\n71|// version. The second result is false for any other major: there is\n72|// no mapping to derive, only the two closed bindings.\n73|func VersionForMajor(major int) (string, bool) {\n74|\tswitch major {\n75|\tcase MajorV1:\n76|\t\treturn \"1.0.0\", true\n77|\tcase MajorV2:\n78|\t\treturn \"2.0.0\", true\n79|\tdefault:\n80|\t\treturn \"\", false\n81|\t}\n82|}\n83|\n84|// MajorForVersion inverts VersionForMajor: only the two exact N.0.0\n85|// versions name a major. Any other version — including a patched\n86|// 2.0.1 — is not a supported major under another spelling.\n87|func MajorForVersion(version string) (int, bool) {\n88|\tswitch version {\n89|\tcase \"1.0.0\":\n90|\t\treturn MajorV1, true\n91|\tcase \"2.0.0\":\n92|\t\treturn MajorV2, true\n93|\tdefault:\n94|\t\treturn 0, false\n95|\t}\n96|}\n97|\n98|// Operation names one Section 7.9 registry entry. The registry is\n99|// closed: dispatch refuses any other name locally, before any node\n100|// surface is touched.\n101|type Operation string\n102|\n103|// Section 7.9 operation registry in the section's table order. The\n104|// inventory test derives this list from the pinned specification\n105|// text and requires exact ordered equality, so a dropped, added, or\n106|// reordered entry reddens there rather than passing silently.\n107|const (\n108|\tOpManifest            Operation = \"manifest\"\n109|\tOpProbe               Operation = \"probe\"\n110|\tOpScan                Operation = \"scan\"\n111|\tOpInventory           Operation = \"inventory\"\n112|\tOpPreview             Operation = \"preview\"\n113|\tOpEnrichmentPlan      Operation = \"enrichment-plan\"\n114|\tOpEnrichmentRun       Operation = \"enrichment-run\"\n115|\tOpEnrichmentStatus    Operation = \"enrichment-status\"\n116|\tOpContinuationInspect Operation = \"continuation-inspect\"\n117|\tOpRuntimeObserve      Operation = \"runtime-observe\"\n118|\tOpDoctor              Operation = \"doctor\"\n119|)\n120|\n121|// operationOrder is the single construction site of the dispatch\n122|// registry.\n123|var operationOrder = []Operation{\n124|\tOpManifest,\n125|\tOpProbe,\n126|\tOpScan,\n127|\tOpInventory,\n128|\tOpPreview,\n129|\tOpEnrichmentPlan,\n130|\tOpEnrichmentRun,\n131|\tOpEnrichmentStatus,\n132|\tOpContinuationInspect,\n133|\tOpRuntimeObserve,\n134|\tOpDoctor,\n135|}\n136|\n137|// Operations returns the dispatch registry in section order. The\n138|// result is a copy; the registry cannot be mutated through it.\n139|func Operations() []string {\n140|\tout := make([]string, 0, len(operationOrder))\n141|\tfor _, operation := range operationOrder {\n142|\t\tout = append(out, string(operation))\n143|\t}\n144|\treturn out\n145|}\n146|\n147|// framedOperations is the scoped subset of the registry this host\n148|// frames in this deliverable: manifest, probe, and scan request\n149|// and success bodies, plus the Session Directory Query contract\n150|// of Section 10.8.5. The remaining eight registry members —\n151|// inventory, preview, enrichment-plan, enrichment-run,\n152|// enrichment-status, continuation-inspect, runtime-observe, and\n153|// doctor — carry nested observation, lineage, enrichment, and\n154|// runtime types whose content owners are the\n155|// shared-environment and boundary leaves of this Story; this\n156|// package frames no body for them, and the inventory test pins\n157|// that boundary by requiring the framed set to equal exactly\n158|// these three names. There is no dispatcher in this package that\n159|// could route around the subset: callers reach only the entry\n160|// points that exist.\n161|var framedOperations = []Operation{\n162|\tOpManifest,\n163|\tOpProbe,\n164|\tOpScan,\n165|}\n166|\n167|// FramedOperations returns the scoped framed subset in section\n168|// order. The result is a copy.\n169|func FramedOperations() []string {\n170|\tout := make([]string, 0, len(framedOperations))\n171|\tfor _, operation := range framedOperations {\n172|\t\tout = append(out, string(operation))\n173|\t}\n174|\treturn out\n175|}\n176|\n177|// validOperation reports whether the name is a registry member.\n178|func validOperation(name string) bool {\n179|\tfor _, operation := range operationOrder {\n180|\t\tif string(operation) == name {\n181|\t\t\treturn true\n182|\t\t}\n183|\t}\n184|\treturn false\n185|}\n186|\n187|// The refusal constructors below are declared as variables so the\n188|// inventory gate can observe every exercised refusal site. Each is\n189|// the single construction site for its failure class; production\n190|// code must not build *axerror.Error any other way.\n191|//\n192|// failInvalid reports a caller error caught before any node surface\n193|// is touched: an unsupported local major, a binding the caller built\n194|// from unobserved facts, a reused attempt process. failViolation\n195|// reports an unusable node frame: an invalid envelope, a body\n196|// outside its closed shape, a mislabeled major, a partial,\n197|// malformed, over-limit, or escaped result. failUnknownOperation\n198|// reports a name outside the closed registry.\n199|// failDowngrade reports the terminal no-common-major outcome with\n200|// incompatible_protocol. failIntegrity reports a binding observation\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c43f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07573-a73b-7be0-abe2-6029bca74ffd"},"sequence":122,"recorded_at":1780531400000239,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"65c281d8-14aa-4def-b705-62e70b4fce66","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"65c281d8-14aa-4def-b705-62e70b4fce66","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"65c281d8-14aa-4def-b705-62e70b4fce66"},"call_id":"call_01a07573e3337db282302c2630763425","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3drr2m/worktree/internal/dirnode/bootstrap.go`.\n1|package dirnode\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axerror\"\n5|)\n6|\n7|// This file owns the Section 7.9 major bootstrap decision: the\n8|// caller enumerates its locally supported majors in strictly\n9|// descending order with one manifest request each, each attempt on a\n10|// fresh process, and only the exact downgrade tuple authorizes the\n11|// next lower attempt.\n12|//\n13|// The decision is a pure function over the attempt outcome, so it is\n14|// testable without spawning processes: DecideBootstrapStep takes the\n15|// request the attempt was issued under, the single response frame if\n16|// the process produced one, and the process exit status, and returns\n17|// exactly one of success (with the validated manifest), authorized\n18|// downgrade (with the next lower major to attempt on a fresh\n19|// process the caller claims in its guard), or a terminal refusal. Process lifecycle —\n20|// launching, terminating, reaping — belongs to the caller; the\n21|// ProcessGuard below is the host check that a returned or failed\n22|// process is never reused for a lower major.\n23|\n24|// BootstrapDecision is one DecideBootstrapStep outcome. Exactly one\n25|// of Manifest, Downgrade, or Terminal carries the verdict: Done\n26|// with a validated manifest whose supported versions contain the\n27|// selected one, Downgrade with the next lower major to attempt on a\n28|// fresh process, or a terminal refusal that must not cause a\n29|// lower-major attempt.\n30|type BootstrapDecision struct {\n31|\tDone      bool\n32|\tManifest  Manifest\n33|\tDowngrade bool\n34|\tNextMajor int\n35|\tTerminal  error\n36|}\n37|\n38|// NextLowerMajor reports the next lower locally supported major to\n39|// attempt. The second result is false when no lower major remains:\n40|// the caller then terminates with its own incompatible_protocol,\n41|// never with a relabeled envelope.\n42|func NextLowerMajor(major int) (int, bool) {\n43|\tfor index, supported := range supportedMajors {\n44|\t\tif supported != major {\n45|\t\t\tcontinue\n46|\t\t}\n47|\t\tif index+1 < len(supportedMajors) {\n48|\t\t\treturn supportedMajors[index+1], true\n49|\t\t}\n50|\t\treturn 0, false\n51|\t}\n52|\treturn 0, false\n53|}\n54|\n55|// isExactDowngradeError reports whether the decoded failure is the\n56|// exact downgrade trigger: Structured Error 1.2\n57|// incompatible_protocol with exit 6 and retryable=false. The\n58|// envelope half of the tuple — one well-framed failure echoing\n59|// protocol, protocol_version, request_id, and operation=manifest\n60|// with response schema_version 1.0.0 — is already established by\n61|// CheckFailureEnvelope before this runs; the process-exit half is\n62|// checked by DecideBootstrapStep against the reaped status. Every\n63|// field is compared: a tuple that names another code, another exit,\n64|// or claims retry permission is an ordinary failure, never\n65|// negotiation evidence.\n66|func isExactDowngradeError(failure *axerror.Error) bool {\n67|\tif failure == nil {\n68|\t\treturn false\n69|\t}\n70|\tif failure.Code() != \"incompatible_protocol\" {\n71|\t\treturn false\n72|\t}\n73|\tif failure.ExitCode() != 6 {\n74|\t\treturn false\n75|\t}\n76|\tif failure.Retryable() {\n77|\t\treturn false\n78|\t}\n79|\treturn true\n80|}\n81|\n82|// ProcessGuard is the host check that a process which returned or\n83|// failed an attempt is never reused for a lower major. The caller\n84|// claims one opaque token per launched process before issuing the\n85|// attempt; claiming the same token twice is a caller error caught\n86|// before any node surface is touched. The zero value is unusable: a\n87|// guard must come from NewProcessGuard so the seen set exists.\n88|type ProcessGuard struct {\n89|\tseen map[string]bool\n90|}\n91|\n92|// NewProcessGuard returns an empty attempt-process guard.\n93|func NewProcessGuard() ProcessGuard {\n94|\treturn ProcessGuard{seen: map[string]bool{}}\n95|}\n96|\n97|// Claim records one attempt process. A token claimed before — a\n98|// returned or failed process offered for a lower major — is\n99|// refused with invalid_config.\n100|func (guard ProcessGuard) Claim(token string) error {\n101|\tif token == \"\" {\n102|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"bootstrap process token is empty\", \"process\")\n103|\t\tif err != nil {\n104|\t\t\treturn err\n105|\t\t}\n106|\t\treturn failure\n107|\t}\n108|\tif guard.seen[token] {\n109|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"bootstrap process was already used for an attempt\", \"process\")\n110|\t\tif err != nil {\n111|\t\t\treturn err\n112|\t\t}\n113|\t\treturn failure\n114|\t}\n115|\tguard.seen[token] = true\n116|\treturn nil\n117|}\n118|\n119|// DecideBootstrapStep decides one manifest attempt. frame carries\n120|// the process's single response line, or is empty when the attempt\n121|// produced no valid response (timeout, signal, exit without one\n122|// valid frame, authentication/allowlist failure at the transport).\n123|// exitStatus is the reaped process status.\n124|//\n125|// Success requires a well-framed success response with every echo\n126|// exact, a complete schema-valid manifest whose\n127|// supported_protocol_versions contains the exact attempted version,\n128|// and process exit 0. The exact downgrade tuple — one well-framed\n129|// failure with incompatible_protocol, exit 6, retryable=false, and\n130|// process exit 6 — authorizes the next lower major when one\n131|// remains, and terminates with the caller's own\n132|// incompatible_protocol when none remains. A wrong or missing echo,\n133|// malformed/partial/extra frame, invalid manifest, timeout, signal,\n134|// nonmatching exit status, or any error other than the exact tuple\n135|// is terminal and never causes a lower-major attempt.\n136|func DecideBootstrapStep(want Request, frame []byte, exitStatus int) BootstrapDecision {\n137|\tif want.Operation != OpManifest {\n138|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"bootstrap attempt does not carry operation manifest\", \"operation\")\n139|\t\tif err != nil {\n140|\t\t\treturn BootstrapDecision{Terminal: err}\n141|\t\t}\n142|\t\treturn BootstrapDecision{Terminal: failure}\n143|\t}\n144|\tif len(frame) == 0 {\n145|\t\tfailure, err := failTransport(\"bootstrap attempt produced no response frame\", \"response\")\n146|\t\tif err != nil {\n147|\t\t\treturn BootstrapDecision{Terminal: err}\n148|\t\t}\n149|\t\treturn BootstrapDecision{Terminal: failure}\n150|\t}\n151|\tif body, err := CheckSuccessEnvelope(frame, want); err == nil {\n152|\t\tmanifest, err := DecodeManifest(body)\n153|\t\tif err != nil {\n154|\t\t\treturn BootstrapDecision{Terminal: err}\n155|\t\t}\n156|\t\tif !manifest.Supports(requestVersion(want)) {\n157|\t\t\tfailure, faultErr := failViolation(\"bootstrap manifest does not contain the attempted version\", \"supported_protocol_versions\")\n158|\t\t\tif faultErr != nil {\n159|\t\t\t\treturn BootstrapDecision{Terminal: faultErr}\n160|\t\t\t}\n161|\t\t\treturn BootstrapDecision{Terminal: failure}\n162|\t\t}\n163|\t\tif exitStatus != 0 {\n164|\t\t\tfailure, faultErr := failViolation(\"bootstrap success carries a nonmatching exit status\", \"exit_status\")\n165|\t\t\tif faultErr != nil {\n166|\t\t\t\treturn BootstrapDecision{Terminal: faultErr}\n167|\t\t\t}\n168|\t\t\treturn BootstrapDecision{Terminal: failure}\n169|\t\t}\n170|\t\treturn BootstrapDecision{Done: true, Manifest: manifest}\n171|\t}\n172|\tfailure, err := CheckFailureEnvelope(frame, want)\n173|\tif err != nil {\n174|\t\treturn BootstrapDecision{Terminal: err}\n175|\t}\n176|\tif !isExactDowngradeError(failure) {\n177|\t\tterminal, terminalErr := failViolation(\"bootstrap failure is not the exact downgrade tuple\", \"error\")\n178|\t\tif terminalErr != nil {\n179|\t\t\treturn BootstrapDecision{Terminal: terminalErr}\n180|\t\t}\n181|\t\treturn BootstrapDecision{Terminal: terminal}\n182|\t}\n183|\tif exitStatus != 6 {\n184|\t\tterminal, terminalErr := failViolation(\"bootstrap downgrade response carries a nonmatching exit status\", \"exit_status\")\n185|\t\tif terminalErr != nil {\n186|\t\t\treturn BootstrapDecision{Terminal: terminalErr}\n187|\t\t}\n188|\t\treturn BootstrapDecision{Terminal: terminal}\n189|\t}\n190|\tnext, ok := NextLowerMajor(want.Major)\n191|\tif !ok {\n192|\t\tterminal, terminalErr := failDowngrade(\"no lower locally supported major remains\", \"protocol_version\")\n193|\t\tif terminalErr != nil {\n194|\t\t\treturn BootstrapDecision{Terminal: terminalErr}\n195|\t\t}\n196|\t\treturn BootstrapDecision{Terminal: terminal}\n197|\t}\n198|\treturn BootstrapDecision{Downgrade: true, NextMajor: next}\n199|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c441","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07573-a73b-7be0-abe2-6029bca74ffd"},"sequence":123,"recorded_at":1780531400000241,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"65c281d8-14aa-4def-b705-62e70b4fce66","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"65c281d8-14aa-4def-b705-62e70b4fce66","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"65c281d8-14aa-4def-b705-62e70b4fce66"},"call_id":"call_01a07573e44270b0b2fde9bc9fa27a6f","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3drr2m/worktree/internal/dirnode/decode.go`.\n1|package dirnode\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"bytes\"\n5|\t\"encoding/json\"\n6|\t\"io\"\n7|\t\"regexp\"\n8|\t\"strings\"\n9|\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n10|\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n12|)\n13|\n14|// This file holds parse-only helpers for every Section 7.9 and\n15|// 10.8.5 closed body. Every helper reports a verdict and never\n16|// refuses: all refusals call one of the refusal constructors\n17|// directly at the deciding site with literal details, so the\n18|// refusal-arm inventory keeps seeing every arm. A helper that\n19|// fronted a constructor would collapse distinct rules into one\n20|// obligation and is not used here.\n21|\n22|// maxUint53 is the largest exactly representable JSON integer:\n23|// Section 7.9 counts and limits are uint53 throughout.\n24|const maxUint53 = uint64(1<<53 - 1)\n25|\n26|// frameFault is one strict-decode failure: what was wrong and which\n27|// member it was found in, if any. It never carries foreign bytes.\n28|type frameFault struct {\n29|\tdetail string\n30|\tmember string\n31|}\n32|\n33|// decodeStrictObject parses one complete JSON object with duplicate\n34|// member rejection. It is the only JSON entry point in this package:\n35|// every body crosses it before any member is read. A non-UTF-8\n36|// frame, a lone surrogate escape, a non-object top level, a\n37|// duplicated member, or trailing data is a fault, never a partial\n38|// object the caller could mistake for a result.\n39|func decodeStrictObject(data []byte) (map[string]json.RawMessage, *frameFault) {\n40|\tif !utf8.Valid(data) {\n41|\t\treturn nil, &frameFault{detail: \"not valid UTF-8\", member: \"\"}\n42|\t}\n43|\tif hasLoneSurrogateEscape(data) {\n44|\t\treturn nil, &frameFault{detail: \"lone surrogate escape\", member: \"\"}\n45|\t}\n46|\tdecoder := json.NewDecoder(bytes.NewReader(data))\n47|\ttoken, err := decoder.Token()\n48|\tif err != nil {\n49|\t\treturn nil, &frameFault{detail: \"not a JSON object\", member: \"\"}\n50|\t}\n51|\tdelim, ok := token.(json.Delim)\n52|\tif !ok || delim != '{' {\n53|\t\treturn nil, &frameFault{detail: \"not a JSON object\", member: \"\"}\n54|\t}\n55|\tmembers := map[string]json.RawMessage{}\n56|\tfor decoder.More() {\n57|\t\tkeyToken, err := decoder.Token()\n58|\t\tif err != nil {\n59|\t\t\treturn nil, &frameFault{detail: \"not a JSON object\", member: \"\"}\n60|\t\t}\n61|\t\tkey, ok := keyToken.(string)\n62|\t\tif !ok {\n63|\t\t\treturn nil, &frameFault{detail: \"not a JSON object\", member: \"\"}\n64|\t\t}\n65|\t\tif _, duplicate := members[key]; duplicate {\n66|\t\t\treturn nil, &frameFault{detail: \"duplicate member\", member: key}\n67|\t\t}\n68|\t\tvar raw json.RawMessage\n69|\t\tif err := decoder.Decode(&raw); err != nil {\n70|\t\t\treturn nil, &frameFault{detail: \"not a JSON object\", member: key}\n71|\t\t}\n72|\t\tmembers[key] = raw\n73|\t}\n74|\tif token, err := decoder.Token(); err != nil {\n75|\t\treturn nil, &frameFault{detail: \"not a JSON object\", member: \"\"}\n76|\t} else if delim, ok := token.(json.Delim); !ok || delim != '}' {\n77|\t\treturn nil, &frameFault{detail: \"not a JSON object\", member: \"\"}\n78|\t}\n79|\tif _, err := decoder.Token(); err != io.EOF {\n80|\t\treturn nil, &frameFault{detail: \"trailing data after the object\", member: \"\"}\n81|\t}\n82|\treturn members, nil\n83|}\n84|\n85|// hasLoneSurrogateEscape reports whether the raw frame carries a\n86|// UTF-16 escape the JSON string grammar cannot pair. Go's\n87|// encoding/json would otherwise replace the lone escape with\n88|// U+FFFD silently, so wire bodies carrying lone surrogates would be\n89|// admitted with rewritten bytes.\n90|func hasLoneSurrogateEscape(data []byte) bool {\n91|\tfor index := 0; index < len(data); index++ {\n92|\t\tif data[index] != '\\\\' {\n93|\t\t\tcontinue\n94|\t\t}\n95|\t\tif index+1 >= len(data) || data[index+1] != 'u' {\n96|\t\t\tcontinue\n97|\t\t}\n98|\t\tfirst, length := readUTF16Escape(data, index+2)\n99|\t\tif length < 0 {\n100|\t\t\treturn true\n101|\t\t}\n102|\t\tindex += 1 + length\n103|\t\tif first >= 0xD800 && first <= 0xDBFF {\n104|\t\t\tsecond, secondLength := readUTF16EscapeAfter(data, index+1)\n105|\t\t\tif secondLength < 0 || second < 0xDC00 || second > 0xDFFF {\n106|\t\t\t\treturn true\n107|\t\t\t}\n108|\t\t\tindex += 6\n109|\t\t\tcontinue\n110|\t\t}\n111|\t\tif first >= 0xDC00 && first <= 0xDFFF {\n112|\t\t\treturn true\n113|\t\t}\n114|\t}\n115|\treturn false\n116|}\n117|\n118|// readUTF16Escape reads four hex digits at the offset. It returns the\n119|// value and the consumed length, or a negative length when the escape\n120|// is truncated or not hexadecimal.\n121|func readUTF16Escape(data []byte, offset int) (uint16, int) {\n122|\tif offset+4 > len(data) {\n123|\t\treturn 0, -1\n124|\t}\n125|\tvar value uint16\n126|\tfor _, digit := range data[offset : offset+4] {\n127|\t\tvalue <<= 4\n128|\t\tswitch {\n129|\t\tcase digit >= '0' && digit <= '9':\n130|\t\t\tvalue |= uint16(digit - '0')\n131|\t\tcase digit >= 'a' && digit <= 'f':\n132|\t\t\tvalue |= uint16(digit-'a') + 10\n133|\t\tcase digit >= 'A' && digit <= 'F':\n134|\t\t\tvalue |= uint16(digit-'A') + 10\n135|\t\tdefault:\n136|\t\t\treturn 0, -1\n137|\t\t}\n138|\t}\n139|\treturn value, 4\n140|}\n141|\n142|// readUTF16EscapeAfter reads a second \\uXXXX escape starting exactly\n143|// at the offset. Anything else is a negative length.\n144|func readUTF16EscapeAfter(data []byte, offset int) (uint16, int) {\n145|\tif offset+6 > len(data) || data[offset] != '\\\\' || data[offset+1] != 'u' {\n146|\t\treturn 0, -1\n147|\t}\n148|\treturn readUTF16Escape(data, offset+2)\n149|}\n150|\n151|// unknownMember names a member outside the closed set, if any. The\n152|// single-unknown fixtures keep the verdict deterministic: with\n153|// several unknowns the map order decides which is named, so tests\n154|// never assert a name from a multi-unknown body.\n155|func unknownMember(members map[string]json.RawMessage, allowed map[string]bool) (string, bool) {\n156|\tfor name := range members {\n157|\t\tif !allowed[name] {\n158|\t\t\treturn name, true\n159|\t\t}\n160|\t}\n161|\treturn \"\", false\n162|}\n163|\n164|// missingMember names the first required member with no value, if\n165|// any. The required list is fixed order, so the verdict is\n166|// deterministic for every missing combination.\n167|func missingMember(members map[string]json.RawMessage, required []string) (string, bool) {\n168|\tfor _, name := range required {\n169|\t\tif _, present := members[name]; !present {\n170|\t\t\treturn name, true\n171|\t\t}\n172|\t}\n173|\treturn \"\", false\n174|}\n175|\n176|// rawString reads a JSON string member.\n177|func rawString(raw json.RawMessage) (string, bool) {\n178|\tvar value string\n179|\tif err := json.Unmarshal(raw, &value); err != nil {\n180|\t\treturn \"\", false\n181|\t}\n182|\treturn value, true\n183|}\n184|\n185|// rawBool reads a JSON boolean member.\n186|func rawBool(raw json.RawMessage) (bool, bool) {\n187|\tvar value bool\n188|\tif err := json.Unmarshal(raw, &value); err != nil {\n189|\t\treturn false, false\n190|\t}\n191|\treturn value, true\n192|}\n193|\n194|// rawUint53 reads an unsigned integral JSON number in [0, 2^53-1]. A\n195|// fraction, exponent, sign, or out-of-range magnitude is not a uint53,\n196|// even when it names the same mathematical value.\n197|func rawUint53(raw json.RawMessage) (uint64, bool) {\n198|\tdecoder := json.NewDecoder(bytes.NewReader(raw))\n199|\tdecoder.UseNumber()\n200|\tvar value any\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
