duction source\n22|// (helper calls with their member, len guards in any statement\n23|// context, DecodeFindings cap instantiations), and\n24|// TestBoundGuardsAreCensused requires the derived multiset to\n25|// equal boundRegistrations exactly. A new bound in one of the\n26|// derived shapes below with no row fails the census; a removed\n27|// bound orphans its row and fails too. A helper alias\n28|// (`var f = requireStringBounds`) fails as an indirection\n29|// violation rather than a missed site. An empty scan fails\n30|// closed. Site identity is file|function|member,\n31|// never the bound values: a moved bound (+1) keeps its identity\n32|// and must redden its behavioral driver, which the mutant battery\n33|// proves per row.\n34|//\n35|// Shape space (review rev6 G-B; the brief asked what shape comes\n36|// after the one just closed, so the answer is written here, not\n37|// left as silence). A bound in this package can only be carried\n38|// by these AST shapes; the census derives the marked ones and\n39|// bounds the rest:\n40|//\n41|//   1. A direct call to one of the six helpers — DERIVED with\n42|//      the bounded member.\n43|//   2. A bound helper through a func-value indirection (var,\n44|//      :=, assignment, argument, return, struct field, method\n45|//      value) — DERIVED as a census violation (the alias\n46|//      itself fails rather than each hidden call).\n47|//   3. A comparison holding a len(...) call in any statement\n48|//      context (if, for, switch, return, assignment) — DERIVED.\n49|//   4. A comparison over a length variable bound from len(...)\n50|//      or stringLength(...) (`n := len(v); if n > 4096`) —\n51|//      DERIVED (review rev6 shape; two live mechanism rows:\n52|//      the shared character-count enforcements in\n53|//      checkStringBounds and checkSortedUniqueStrings).\n54|//   5. A comparison holding a direct stringLength(...) call —\n55|//      DERIVED by the same rule (no live instance today; the\n56|//      only production length measures flow through named\n57|//      variables).\n58|//   6. A bound inside a package-level var initializer,\n59|//      including func literals — DERIVED under the variable\n60|//      name (review rev6 shape; zero live rows today, proven by\n61|//      the synthetic package-literal test below).\n62|//   7. Cross-field relational gates (maxObjects >\n63|//      maxTotalBytes and its sibling in DecodeResourceLimits) —\n64|//      STATED: not edge-valued sites, pinned behaviourally by\n65|//      TestDecodeResourceLimitsBounds instead.\n66|//   8. The maxUint53 maxima — STATED: representability bounds\n67|//      pinned once by TestUint53RepresentabilityCeiling rather\n68|//      than per site.\n69|//   9. A comparison over a decoded value or caller-supplied\n70|//      number with no length source in the function (`value <\n71|//      minimum` over a rawUint53 result, a plain int parameter)\n72|//      — STATED BOUND, not derived. Live instance:\n73|//      checkUint53Bounds (decode.go:269); the bound is enforced\n74|//      at every caller row, and every caller row carries a\n75|//      driver or a pinned exemption.\n76|//  10. A direct cap(...) or utf8.RuneCountInString(...)\n77|//      comparison outside stringLength — STATED BOUND, not\n78|//      derived. No live instance: the only production\n79|//      rune-count use is inside stringLength, whose callers are\n80|//      all rostered rows.\n81|//\n82|// 6 of 10 shapes derived, 2 stated-pinned, 2 stated bounds. A new\n83|// bound in shapes 1-6 with no row fails\n84|// TestBoundGuardsAreCensused; shapes 7-8 are pinned once each by\n85|// their named suite; shapes 9-10 are the named residue.\n86|//\n87|// Every non-exempt row names its driver: the committed test\n88|// proving refusal at its edges (min-1/max+1) through the\n89|// production entry. Admission at the accepted edge itself is\n90|// proven only where the driver says so: 21 rows drive the\n91|// refusal side only (review rev6 accept-direction battery), and\n92|// that is recorded here as a bound rather than claimed per site.\n93|// Exempt rows say why: equivalent (the bound is unreachable\n94|// behind an upstream gate), stated-bound (a 65537-element body),\n95|// mechanism (transparent forwarder or generic guard whose values\n96|// live at the caller rows), or plumbing (byte-scanner loop\n97|// guards pinned by the surrogate agreement suite).\n98|//\n99|// Stated bounds of this census: shapes 7-10 above, plus the\n100|// refusal-side-only drivers. _test.go files, which never ship,\n101|// are outside the derivation, as are const initializers, which\n102|// hold no calls and whose constant comparisons are vacuous.\n103|\n104|import (\n105|\t\"bytes\"\n106|\t\"encoding/json\"\n107|\t\"fmt\"\n108|\t\"go/ast\"\n109|\t\"go/parser\"\n110|\t\"go/printer\"\n111|\t\"go/token\"\n112|\t\"os\"\n113|\t\"path/filepath\"\n114|\t\"sort\"\n115|\t\"strconv\"\n116|\t\"strings\"\n117|\t\"testing\"\n118|)\n119|\n120|// boundRegistration is one production bound site with its proof:\n121|// the behavioral driver covering its edges, or an explicit\n122|// exemption with its rationale.\n123|type boundRegistration struct {\n124|\tid     string\n125|\tdriver string\n126|\texempt bool\n127|\treason string\n128|}\n129|\n130|// boundHelpers is the closed helper set the census derives. A\n131|// seventh bound helper with no row here fails the census only if\n132|// it is called; the call-shape derivation below names the helper\n133|// per site, so an unrostered helper surfaces as unregistered\n134|// sites.\n135|var boundHelpers = map[string]bool{\n136|\t\"checkStringBounds\":        true,\n137|\t\"requireStringBounds\":      true,\n138|\t\"checkUint53Bounds\":        true,\n139|\t\"requireUint53Bounds\":      true,\n140|\t\"checkSortedUniqueStrings\": true,\n141|\t\"checkSortedUniqueDigests\": true,\n142|}\n143|\n144|// scanBoundSiteIDs derives every bound site identity from\n145|// production source: file|function|helper|member|ordinal for the\n146|// six helpers and DecodeFindings instantiations, and\n147|// file|function|len|rendered|ordinal for len guards in any\n148|// statement context (if, for, switch, return, assignment —\n149|// review rev5/F2), including guards over length variables bound\n150|// from len(...) or stringLength(...) and guards holding a direct\n(more lines below)"}}}
