{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d803","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07573-a73b-7be0-abe2-6029bca74ffd"},"sequence":2652,"recorded_at":1780531400005299,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"65c281d8-14aa-4def-b705-62e70b4fce66","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"65c281d8-14aa-4def-b705-62e70b4fce66","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"65c281d8-14aa-4def-b705-62e70b4fce66"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"b516f3e9-6c48-4a18-a64d-7504864943a6"},"task_id":"b516f3e9-6c48-4a18-a64d-7504864943a6","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"b516f3e9-6c48-4a18-a64d-7504864943a6","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-06\n-\n-### 0930 — Directory-node leaf: `internal/dirnode` implemented with enumerated census first\n+## 2026-09-06\n+\n+### 1035 — Directory-node leaf round-2 rework: rev1 B1/B2/B3 closed, 185-mutant battery\n+\n+- SCOPE: TASK-260830-ljkj8r round-2 rework (review-verdict-rev1, changes requested, B1–B3 blocking). Test-only additions inside `internal/dirnode/` (`bound_census_test.go`, `bounds_edge_test.go`, `query_operations_test.go`, `arm_identity_test.go`) plus four one-line fixture-surgery fixes (`query_test.go` unknown_field + missing caller, `manifest_test.go` missing member, `probe_test.go` missing member) and three edge extensions (findings 4097, cursor 1/1024 admission, projection bound edges). No production behavior change. Uncommitted per the CR-shape instruction.\n+- FIX (B1): bound census ported from the sessadapter leaf — 101 production-derived sites (9 helpers + len/length-var guards, 10-shape space with 6 derived + 4 stated), 72 driven + 29 exempt mechanism/plumbing. Edge drivers prove min-1/min/max/max+1 through the production entry. Battery: 185 applied / 142 behavioural kills / 43 equivalent-with-bound / 0 survivors, zero not-applied, zero compile failures. Census-only kills scored separately (2 live census mutants + 3 synthetic gate proofs).\n+- FIX (B2): `TestDecodeQueryAllOperationsAdmit` drives 17/17 registry operations (was 5/17); 40+ validator defects through DecodeQuery including the review probes environments/\"root\", jobs/\"pwned\", distinct/\"secret\" (battery V01–V03, all killed). Zero functions at 0.0% (was 10, all §10.8.5 validators).\n+- FIX (B3): unknown_field rebuilt without the duplicate member + reachability proof; audit found the same rename-instead-of-delete slide in three more missing vectors, all fixed to deletions + message-identity proof. Protocol relabeled-major placeholder verified genuine (overridden with a real relabeled frame).\n+- FINDINGS: (1) Closed vocabularies mask bound narrowings — 11 count ceilings equal their vocabulary size (no ceiling+1 member buildable) and 20 element bounds cannot discriminate behind the outer gate; all recorded as equivalents, never survivors. (2) Count/index gates coincide at the 65th operation — each single weakening is masked behind the other; pinned jointly. (3) Test scaffolds must not size probes from production constants: the frame suite initially referenced MaxFrameBytes and went green under a widened constant; now retyped (frameBoundBytes) like all fixtures. Same fix applied to two protocol oversize vectors and the uint53 ceiling probe.\n+- EVIDENCE: attached TASK-260830-ljkj8r_round2.md (verdicts, equivalence classes, full 185-row table, 9/9 AC mapping). Production files byte-identical (battery is copy-back per mutant; post-run grep for mutant literals clean).\n+- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (18 pkgs), `-race` on dirnode exit 0, `go vet ./...` and `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=94, unchanged). Dirnode cover 74.9% → 83.3%.\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off uncommitted.\n+\n+### 0930 — Directory-node leaf: `internal/dirnode` implemented with enumerated census first\n"}}}
